  "description": "Age-standardised incidence rate of all cancers combined per 100,000 population. Despite an ageing population, the overall rate has been stable or declining slightly since 2000.",
  "explainer": "Australia has one of the highest cancer incidence rates in the world \u2014 partly reflecting ageing population, high UV exposure and good detection. The age-standardised rate tells a nuanced story: despite an ageing population the overall rate has declined slightly since 2000, driven by falling lung cancer (reduced smoking) and improved prevention. Melanoma continues to rise. Five-year survival has improved from 47% in the 1980s to over 70% today \u2014 cancer is increasingly a chronic condition.",
